// "meld <subject> into <name>" [CR#701.42a]: combine two specific permanents
// you control into a single melded permanent. Lean `meldInto`.
//
// STOP (updated by `semantics-v2-macro-param-kinds`): the melded
// permanent's name is Lean's own `String`. `deckmaste_semantics_v2::ron::
// param_types()` already registers `String` (it comes from `macro_ron`
// itself), but `deckmaste_construction_core::macro_def::ParameterType` — the
// SAME closed eight-name enum {Ability, Amount, Condition, Cost, Power,
// Quality, Subject, Toughness}, mirrored independently on the
// english_v2/typed side that reads every `plugins_v2` declaration's
// `params:` field too (§11: neither crate depends on the other for the
// shared declaration file, so BOTH readers must accept a param type before
// any declaration can use it) — has no `String` variant either and was out
// of this ticket's authorized file scope. A one-sided fix is unusable
// (`both_readers_accept_every_builtin_declaration` fails from the
// construction_core side alone). Left bodyless pending that companion fix.
KeywordAction(
    name: "Meld",
    spelling: "meld",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "meld",
        frame_set: Transitive,
    ),
)
